  "Tasted bland" means you're already at the maximum Int for your
character.  Natural Int of 20 means you're an Elf.  To get past that
wear an enchanted Helm of Brilliance.  

  In addition to the regular advantages of extra Int and Wis there's a
threshold at (Int+Wis) greater than 45.  After that point Pw
regeneration is a little higher.  It's a one-shot change.  Increasing
(Int+Wis) more once you're above 45 doesn't add any more power
regeneration, although you still get the normal Int and Wis benefits.


  A point about power regeneration:  You want to do it as much as
possible.  When you're at maximum Pw you're not generating any more
mana.  So whenever you hit max, cast a spell.  (This is a great way to
improve skill in spell schools.)

  

